          <div class="cs-subsection">
            <div>
              <span class="cs-subsection-subheading uppercase">
                <span class="en">Decision 01</span>
                <span class="fr">Décision 01</span>
              </span>
              <h3 class="cs-subsection-heading">
                <span class="en">Every dataset, clearly labeled</span>
                <span class="fr">Tous les datasets, clairement identifiés</span>
              </h3>
              <div class="grid-2 items-baseline cs-de-decision">
                <div>
                  <p class="cs-de-answers">
                    <span class="cs-de-answers-label"
                      ><span class="en">Data strategy</span><span class="fr"
                        >Stratégie data</span
                      ></span
                    >
                    <span class="cs-de-answers-text">
                      <span class="en"
                        >20,000+ datasets, unreviewed included</span
                      >
                      <span class="fr"
                        >Plus de 20&nbsp;000 datasets, non validés compris</span
                      >
                    </span>
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-de-decision-body">
                  <p class="en">
                    The strategy was to open all 20,000+ datasets, but only
                    reviewed ones can be used to start an analysis. I made that
                    difference visible in the list and in the filters: a Status
                    column tags each dataset, <span
                      class="cs-de-tag"
                      data-tone="reviewed">Reviewed</span
                    > in green and <span
                      class="cs-de-tag"
                      data-tone="unreviewed">Unreviewed</span
                    > in gray, and a checkbox in the filters shows reviewed datasets
                    only.
                  </p>
                  <p class="fr">
                    La stratégie était d'ouvrir les plus de 20&nbsp;000
                    datasets, mais seuls les datasets validés permettent de
                    lancer une analyse. J'ai rendu cette différence visible dans
                    la liste et dans les filtres&nbsp;: une colonne Status
                    étiquette chaque dataset, en vert pour <span
                      class="cs-de-tag"
                      data-tone="reviewed">Reviewed</span
                    > et en gris pour <span
                      class="cs-de-tag"
                      data-tone="unreviewed">Unreviewed</span
                    >, et une case à cocher dans les filtres permet de
                    n'afficher que les validés.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-img">
              <img
